{#
Args:
    kernels: A dictionary of kernel analysis results, where the key is the kernel name and the value is an object containing the analysis results for that kernel.
        The structure of the dictionary is as follows:
        {
            "kernel_name": {
                "runtime": float,  # The average runtime of the kernel in milliseconds
                "launch_config": str,  # The launch configuration of the kernel (e.g., "[SIMD32 {1000,1,1} {256,1,1}]")
                "thread_occupancy": float,  # The thread occupancy of the kernel in percentage
                "bound": str,  # The bottleneck type of the kernel, either "compute", "memory", or "balanced"
                "alu_util": [  # A list of ALU utilization objects, sorted by utilization percentage in descending order
                    {
                        "name": str,  # The name of the ALU resource (e.g., "ALU0", "ALU1", etc.)
                        "util_pct": float,  # The utilization percentage of this ALU resource
                        "instr_mix": [  # A list of instruction mix objects for this ALU resource
                            {
                                "name": str,  # The name of the instruction type (e.g., "FP16", "INT64", etc.)
                                "pct": float,  # The percentage of this instruction type in the instruction mix for this ALU resource
                            },
                            ...
                        ],
                    },
                    ...
                ],
                "gmem_bandwidth_pct": float,  # The percentage of peak global memory bandwidth utilized by the kernel
                "slm_bandwidth_pct": float,  # The percentage of peak shared local memory bandwidth utilized by the kernel
                "ve_stall_pct": float,  # The percentage of time vector engines are stalled waiting for memory operations to complete
                "slm_conflicts_pct": float,  # The percentage of shared local memory accesses causing bank conflicts
            },
            ...
        }
#}
{% for kernel_name, k in kernels.items() %}
## Analysis of kernel {{ kernel_name }}:

### Runtime and Occupancy:
The launch configuration of the kernel is {{ k.launch_config }}.
The average runtime of the kernel is {{ "{:.2f}".format(k.runtime) }} ms.
{% if k.thread_occupancy %}
The thread occupancy is {{ "{:.2f}".format(k.thread_occupancy) }}%.
{% endif %}
The vector engine stall rate is {{ "{:.2f}".format(k.ve_stall_pct) }}%

### Roofline Analysis:
{% if k.bound == 'compute' %}
The kernel is using compute more than memory bandwidth.
{% elif k.bound == 'memory' %}
The kernel is using memory bandwidth more than compute. 
{% else %}
The kernel is balanced between compute and memory bandwidth. 
{% endif %}
The highest utilized compute resource is {{ k.alu_util[0].name }} with {{ "{:.2f}".format(k.alu_util[0].util_pct) }}% utilization.
The utilized global memory bandwidth is {{ "{:.2f}".format(k.gmem_bandwidth_pct) }}% of the peak memory bandwidth. 
{% if k.slm_bandwidth_pct > 0 and k.slm_bandwidth_pct > k.gmem_bandwidth_pct %}
The utilized shared local memory bandwidth is {{ "{:.2f}".format(k.slm_bandwidth_pct) }}% of the peak SLM bandwidth.
{% endif %}

### Bottleneck Analysis:
{% if k.bound == 'compute' %}
{% set compute_breakdown_block %}
{{ k.alu_util[0].name }} is the highest utilized compute resource with {{ "{:.2f}".format(k.alu_util[0].util_pct) }}% utilization, which is likely the bottleneck for this kernel.
The instruction mix is:
    {% for instr in k.alu_util[0].instr_mix %}
        {% if instr.pct > 0 %}
- {{ instr.name }}: {{ "{:.2f}".format(instr.pct) }}%
        {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% for alu in k.alu_util[1:] %}

        {% if alu.util_pct > 0 %}
The utilization of {{ alu.name }} is {{ "{:.2f}".format(alu.util_pct) }}%. 
The instruction mix is:
            {% for instr in alu.instr_mix %}
                {% if instr.pct > 0 %}
- {{ instr.name }}: {{ "{:.2f}".format(instr.pct) }}%
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
        {% else %}
            {% if alu.name == "ALU2" %}
ALU2 providing hardware acceleration for matrix multiplications with XMX instructions is not utilized.
            {% else %}
{{ alu.name }} ({% for instr in alu.instr_mix %}{{ instr.name }}{{ ", " if not loop.last else "" }}{% endfor %}) is not utilized.
            {% endif %}
        {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
{% endset %}
{{ compute_breakdown_block }}
To improve compute performance try to shift the instruction mix towards more efficient instructions or better balance the utilization of different compute resources.
{% elif k.bound == 'memory' %}
{% set memory_breakdown_block %}
The kernel's global memory bandwidth is {{"{:.2f}".format(k.gmem_bandwidth) }} GB/s, which is {{ "{:.2f}".format(k.gmem_bandwidth_pct) }}% of the peak bandwidth.
The vector engines are stalled for {{ "{:.2f}".format(k.ve_stall_pct) }}% of the time likely waiting for memory operations to complete.
{% if k.slm_bandwidth_pct == 0 %}
The kernel does not make use of shared local memory. Consider using shared local memory to reduce global memory bandwidth pressure.
{% elif k.slm_bandwidth_pct > 70 %}
The kernel is heavily utilizing shared local memory ({{ "{:.2f}".format(k.slm_bandwidth_pct) }}% of the peak shared local memory bandwidth), which may be a bottleneck.
{% endif %}
{% if k.slm_bandwidth_pct > 0 and k.slm_conflicts_pct > 0%}
The percentage of shared local memory accesses causing bank conflicts is {{ "{:.2f}".format(k.slm_conflicts_pct) }}%. 
Consider optimizing shared local memory access patterns to reduce bank conflicts.
{% endif %}
{% endset %}
{{ memory_breakdown_block }}
{% else %}
The kernel is balanced between compute and memory bandwidth. 
To improve performance compute and memory bandwidth should be improved together.
{{ compute_breakdown_block }}
{{ memory_breakdown_block }}
{% endif %}


{% endfor %}